ther national Democratic surrogates and outside spending shift the race away from its narrow tie.", "confidence": "low", "notes": []}, "overview": "Florida's 22nd is an open seat created by redrawing, with a Republican-leaning partisan baseline but a strong Democratic national environment in 2026. Casey Askar has raised about $2.6 million and drawn outside opposition spending, while Pia Dandiya has raised about $2.3 million with slightly more cash on hand and has launched her first general election TV ads.\n\nExpert ratings split between Lean R (flip) calls from several outlets and Lean D or Tossup calls from others, and the few available polls show a race within the margin of error, with Dandiya narrowly ahead in the most recent surveys. Prediction markets price the contest near even. National Democrats are stumping in the district, signaling both sides see it as winnable.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5161, "margin": 0.22}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4293, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5493, "margin": 0.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5402, "margin": 0.2}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4658, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4995, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.5432, "margin": 0.5}]}